These commands synchronize your local repository with GitHub.

git push	Upload commits to GitHub
git push origin main	Push main branch
git push -u origin main	Push and set upstream
git pull	Download and integrate remote changes
git pull origin main	Pull changes from main
git fetch	Download remote updates without merging
git fetch --all	Fetch from all remotes
git push --force-with-lease	Safely attempt a force push

Difference between fetch and pull:
- fetch = Download remote updates.
- pull = Fetch + integrate changes into your current branch.
